rogated violently beaten  strangled and literally shocked for days  on end  yet he remained conscious and of course  refused to divulge any information  at the end of this ordeal after he was  rescued doctors said that it would take  weeks for him to recover  or even be able to walk but instead  fischer climbs to his feet  and immediately gets back to work there  has even been one situation in blacklist  where he was exposed to a nerve agent  but he managed to resist the effects for  a considerable amount of time  while he finished off the job of killing  a bunch of bad guys before passing out  shortly after while these two characters  are obviously complete badasses  the conclusion of who would win is  pretty clear-cut to me  john wick is a complete crack shot with  any weapon he gets his hands on  and in close combat he can more than  hold his own but sam  fisher has all of this and more his  training  background experience the state of the  art tech he utilizes  but probably most importantly his  techniques and tactics  particularly in regards to his use of  stealth wick would be taken down before  he was even aware of fish's location  even if he was allowed to see him first  i know there's going to be a bunch of  comments from people who are die-hard  fans of the john wick series  saying that it would be a much closer  fight but all i have to go on is the  movies  books games and any other fact-checked  information i can find online  and everything points towards sam fisher  absolutely dominating john wick  in every way a splinter cell agent  is the equivalent of an entire black ops  squad on their own  their main purpose is to infiltrate  impenetrable locations  and make it out of even the most  impossible scenarios  they're trained to perform the  impossible they're experts in the art of  stealth  and have peak human physicality and the  skill to make most men on the  battlefield look like uncoordinated  children  even without the high-tech gear fischer  has proven to be the elite among the  elite  in conviction he went up against  splinter cells that he had trained  himself  and while they had all the gear he was  still able to take them out with ease  where john wick tends to spend more of  his time walking in completely oblivious  to the idea of taking cover  getting shot stabbed and beaten to hell  by almost every group of thugs and  gangsters that he comes across  yes he is god-like precision but even if  fischer wasn't quite to the same level  his movement on the battlefield more  than makes up for this  he is constantly keeping tabs of his  environment and the people around him  making backup plans in the middle of  executing one and is always aware of  everything around him so that he stays  one step ahead  sam fischer is more well known to the  bulk of you watching this due to his  time as a video game character  and the only weaknesses he's shown over  the years has purely been done for game  balancing purposes  even his age isn't slowing him down yet  in case you couldn't tell i was a little  surprised by the number of requests for  this versus video  as someone who has watched the movies  and played most of the games the answer  seemed fairly obvious to me  but i enjoyed making this especially  since i had a good reason to watch the  movies again  so thank you for the suggestion i have  plenty more to catch up on but keep  firing away i should get to them  eventually otherwise thank you very much  for watching and i'll catch in the next  one  [Music]  [Applause]  cheers  [Music]  thank you
 

